@prefix cme: <http://example.org/cme#> .
@prefix chx: <http://example.org/sen0401/ch06#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/sen0401/ch06/diagrams> a owl:Ontology ; rdfs:label "SEN0401 ch06 narrative diagrams - ABox"@en ; owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; dcterms:identifier "sen0401_ch06_diagrams_abox_v1_0_0" ;
    rdfs:comment "The chapter's authored diagrams as cme:NarrativeDiagram individuals: generated by sen0401_page_data_v2_11_0.py from sen0401_ch06_diagrams_v1_0_0.py, typed by the CME narrative-to-diagram mapping (a module of cme_standards_adoption_v1_3_0.ttl, CME 0.16.0)."@en ; owl:imports <http://example.org/cme/narrative-diagram> .

chx:Diagram_ParseTransaction a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Reading a serialized transaction, field by field"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6, A serialized Bitcoin transaction and its parts: the version (4 bytes), the marker 0x00 and the flag 0x01 of the extended format, the input count as a compactSize integer, each input's outpoint, input script and sequence, the output count, each output's amount and output script, one witness stack per input, and the lock time; the legacy format has no marker, flag or witness" ; cme:elementCount 18 ;
    cme:accompanies "TransactionAnatomy" ; cme:accompanies "SerializationFormats" ; cme:accompanies "SerializedTransaction" ; cme:accompanies "ExtendedFormat" ; cme:accompanies "LegacyFormat" ; cme:accompanies "ByteMap" ; cme:accompanies "TransactionParts" ; cme:accompanies "MarkerByte" ; cme:accompanies "FlagByte" ; cme:accompanies "InputCount" ; cme:accompanies "OutputCount" ; cme:accompanies "WitnessStack" ; rdfs:comment "the chapter walks the bytes in order, with one decision - is the byte after the version a zero marker? - and a loop over the counted inputs and outputs: a workflow"@en .
chx:Diagram_TransactionFields a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "A transaction and its fields"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:TopicAndParts ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:MindMap ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6, the parts of a transaction: the version, in the extended format a marker and a flag, the inputs field (a count, then for each input an outpoint, a length-prefixed input script and a sequence), the outputs field (a count, then for each output an amount and a length-prefixed output script), the witness structure (one stack per input, counted items) and the lock time" ; cme:elementCount 21 ;
    cme:accompanies "TransactionIdea" ; cme:accompanies "Transaction" ; cme:accompanies "TransactionParts" ; cme:accompanies "OwnershipRecord" ; cme:accompanies "VersionField" ; cme:accompanies "InputList" ; cme:accompanies "OutputList" ; cme:accompanies "WitnessSerialization" ; cme:accompanies "LockTime" ; rdfs:comment "the chapter lays out one subject, the serialized transaction, by its fields and the fields inside them - a topic and its parts"@en .
chx:Diagram_CardGameChannel a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Alice and Bob's card game: the original payment channel"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Interaction ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:SequenceDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6, Original sequence-based transaction replacement: the setup transaction into a multisignature output, the refund with sequence 0 that neither broadcasts, the rounds of the card game in which the sequence is incremented and the balances move, the final version with sequence 0xffffffff that is broadcast, relayed and confirmed, and the alternative scenario in which Bob broadcasts an earlier version" ; cme:elementCount 12 ;
    cme:accompanies "SequenceReplacement" ; cme:accompanies "SequenceNumber" ; cme:accompanies "SetupTransaction" ; cme:accompanies "PaymentChannel" ; cme:accompanies "ReplacementAttack" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is an exchange between Alice, Bob and the network in an order that matters - deposit, refund, rounds, final version, and an old version that nodes refuse: an interaction"@en .
chx:Diagram_TransactionLife a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "The life of a transaction, from signing to confirmation"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:LifeCycle ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:StateDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6: Protecting presigned transactions (signed but not broadcast, for months or years), Opt-in transaction replacement signaling (an unconfirmed transaction with the BIP125 signal may be replaced by a conflicting one paying a higher fee rate), Lock time (eligible for any block, or only from a height or a time), Sequence as a relative timelock (confirmed only once the spent output has aged), the rule against double spending (only one of two conflicting transactions can be in a valid blockchain)" ; cme:elementCount 16 ;
    cme:accompanies "PresignedTransaction" ; cme:accompanies "ReplaceByFee" ; cme:accompanies "OptInRbf" ; cme:accompanies "Bip125Signal" ; cme:accompanies "ConflictingTransactions" ; cme:accompanies "LockTimeField" ; cme:accompanies "RelativeTimelock" ; cme:accompanies "Bip68Timelock" ; cme:accompanies "RelayPolicy" ; cme:accompanies "ConsensusRule" ; rdfs:comment "the passages describe the states a transaction is in over time and the events that move it - signed, held, broadcast, replaced, confirmed, or refused as a conflict: a life cycle"@en .
chx:Diagram_MalleabilityAttack a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Third-party malleability: a stranger changes the txid, Bob's payment to Carol fails"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Interaction ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:SequenceDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6, Third-party transaction malleability: Alice creates a transaction with OP_2 in the input script paying Bob, Bob immediately spends that output to Carol, anyone on the network replaces OP_2 with OP_PUSH1 0x02 creating a conflict with a different txid; if the conflicting version is confirmed, Alice's original cannot be, and Bob's transaction cannot spend its output - and Segregated witness: an empty input script keeps witnesses from affecting the txid" ; cme:elementCount 12 ;
    cme:accompanies "MalleabilityProblems" ; cme:accompanies "ThirdPartyMalleability" ; cme:accompanies "PushEncoding" ; cme:accompanies "CircularDependency" ; cme:accompanies "SecondPartyMalleability" ; cme:accompanies "Segwit" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is an exchange between Alice, Bob, Carol, a third party and the network, in an order that decides who loses: an interaction"@en .
chx:Diagram_WhoUsesTransactions a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Who works with a transaction, and for what"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:SetOfUses ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:UseCaseDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6: a transaction as the data Alice uses to convince full nodes to update their database; the full node that looks up the outpoint, obtains the amount and the conditions, checks for double spending and updates its UTXO database; the miner who creates the coinbase and claims the fees and the subsidy; the software that measures a transaction's weight; the relay policy a node applies to unconfirmed transactions; and the contract protocols that presign transactions" ; cme:elementCount 13 ;
    cme:accompanies "OwnershipRecord" ; cme:accompanies "OutpointField" ; cme:accompanies "UtxoDatabase" ; cme:accompanies "DoubleSpendRule" ; cme:accompanies "CoinbaseTransaction" ; cme:accompanies "Coinbase" ; cme:accompanies "BlockReward" ; cme:accompanies "WeightUnits" ; cme:accompanies "Weight" ; cme:accompanies "Foundations" ; cme:accompanies "RelayPolicy" ; rdfs:comment "the chapter tells what the different people and programs do with a transaction - build, sign, relay, validate, mine, measure - a set of uses by actors"@en .
chx:Diagram_SoftForkSegwit a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Deploying segregated witness as a soft fork"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6, Segregated witness: the obvious method requires a hard fork, not compatible with older full nodes; the alternative of late 2015 uses a soft fork, a backward-compatible change under which newer nodes may reject blocks older nodes accept but not the reverse; the approach is based on anyone-can-spend output scripts - a number 0 to 16 followed by 2 to 40 bytes is the segwit template; old nodes allow an empty input script, new nodes require one, and the witness goes in the new witness structure" ; cme:elementCount 10 ;
    cme:accompanies "SegregatedWitness" ; cme:accompanies "HardFork" ; cme:accompanies "SoftFork" ; cme:accompanies "WitnessProgram" ; cme:accompanies "WitnessStructure" ; cme:accompanies "AnyoneCanSpend" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is a procedure with one decision - change the rules in a way old nodes reject, or in a way they accept - and the steps that follow the second branch: a workflow"@en .
